<h2>Who I am</h2>
<p>{{ site.name }} is run by {{ site.owner }} in {{ site.base }}, {{ site.county }}. You can contact me about your data at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> or on {{ site.phone }}.</p>
<h2>What I collect</h2>
<p>When you fill in my form, I collect your name, phone number, email (if given), postcode, town and the details you share about your problem. I use this only to reply to you and arrange help.</p>
<p>Form messages are processed by my website host, Netlify, and delivered to me by email.</p>
<h2>When I visit or connect remotely</h2>
<p>I only access your devices and files with your permission and only as far as needed to fix the problem. I don't copy or keep your personal files unless you ask me to, for example when moving data to a new computer.</p>
<h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
<p>This website never uses advertising cookies.</p>
<p>If you click Accept on the cookie banner, I use Google Analytics (loaded through Google Tag Manager) to see how people find and use the site, such as which pages are popular. It sets cookies (named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_</code> followed by an ID) that last up to two years. Google processes this information for me, and it may be handled outside the UK under Google's standard safeguards. You can read more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
<p>If you click Reject, or don't choose, Google Analytics doesn't load and no cookies are set. You can change your mind at any time using the "Cookie settings" link at the bottom of every page. Your choice is remembered in your browser so I don't ask on every visit.</p>
<p>I also use Umami, a privacy-friendly analytics service, to count visits. It sets no cookies, doesn't collect personal information and doesn't follow you across other websites.</p>
<p>The map on my Areas page is loaded from OpenStreetMap. Like any website you visit, their servers see your IP address when the map tiles load, but they set no cookies.</p>
<h2>How long I keep it</h2>
<p>I keep enquiry and job details for as long as needed to provide the service and meet legal and accounting requirements, then delete them.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You can ask to see, correct or delete the information I hold about you at any time. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).</p>
